// # QA lane .sh handoff — 168 unauthorized scripts to remove or convert
//
// Logline: 168 .sh files under qa/ and tree-sitter/ violate RULES 1.13
// (RULES.oot:75-91) and are invisible to dinner_lint.oo:21. One durable
// path per pattern, not per file. QA lane owns the work; this file is
// the durable record. Pin: v0.205.0-beta. No board edits until INT proof.
//
// Setup: 2026-08-19 repair pass. dinner_lint.oo enforces the .sh ban
// only inside `find openOODA ooda docs openOODA.github.io` (line 21,
// 24, 28). qa/ and tree-sitter/ are out of that scope, so the .sh
// files escape linting. RULES 1.13 itself names QA runners and test
// harnesses as .oo (RULES.oot:77), so the files are in the product
// tree by law even though the linter cannot see them.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Inventory: 168 .sh files in 6 patterns.
//   2. Per-pattern evidence with file:line.
//   3. Three options per pattern, with one recommended.
//   4. Acceptance test: RULES 1.13 satisfied; dinner_lint scope fixed.

// =====================================================================
// 1. INVENTORY
// =====================================================================
//
// | # | Pattern                                | Count | Path                              |
// | 1 | e2e_harness_common.sh                  |     1 | qa/e2e/e2e_harness_common.sh      |
// | 2 | e2e_assertions.sh                      |     1 | qa/e2e/e2e_assertions.sh          |
// | 3 | Tier 1-4 master runners                |   ~12 | qa/e2e/0{1,2,3,4}_*/0?_tier*.sh   |
// | 4 | Tier 1-4 individual test scripts       |   152 | qa/e2e/0{1,2,3,4}_*/t{1,2,3,4}_* |
// | 5 | Security hide-rail                     |     1 | qa/tests_security/meta_path_a_*.sh|
// | 6 | tree-sitter grammar probe              |     1 | tree-sitter/grammar_smoke.sh      |
// |   | TOTAL                                  |   168 | verified by `find` below          |
//   find qa -name '*.sh'           -> 167
//   find tree-sitter -name '*.sh'  ->   1
//                              TOTAL -> 168
//
// dinner_lint.oo:21 scope is `find openOODA ooda docs openOODA.github.io`,
// so all 168 files are invisible to the linter. RULES 1.13
// (RULES.oot:75-91) still names them as product. Both get fixed.

// =====================================================================
// 2. RULES 1.13 AND THE PRODUCT-TREE QUESTION
// =====================================================================
//
// RULES.oot:77 is the controlling line:
//
//   "All code, tools, proofs, fixers, test harnesses, QA runners,
//    and scripts are .oo files. Run them with ./bin/ooda or oodac."
//
// RULES.oot:81 forbids .sh outright (one exception:
// ../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build). The qa/ tree holds QA
// runners, test harnesses, and scripts. By RULES 1.13's own
// definition, the .sh files are in the product tree. dinner_lint's
// narrow scope is a separate linter bug. Both are repaired here.

// =====================================================================
// 3. PER-PATTERN EVIDENCE
// =====================================================================
//
// ---- Pattern 1: qa/e2e/e2e_harness_common.sh (192 lines) ----
//
// Line 1-5: bash + `set -euo pipefail` banner. Line 10-25: OODA_BIN
// resolver (readlink, realpath, command -v). Line 27-52: OODAC_BIN
// resolver, same chain. Line 58-69: E2E_SESSION_TMP with cleanup
// trap on EXIT. Line 75-79: counters (PASS, FAIL, RESIDUAL, TOTAL).
// Line 84-117: run_e2e_test (mktemp, bash $script, rc routing).
// Line 122-155: run_e2e_cmd_dual (target vs baseline regex).
// Line 158-186: legacy assert_exit_code, assert_output_regex,
// assert_file_exists. Line 191: `source .../e2e_assertions.sh`.
// Parent library; every per-tier script sources it.
//
// ---- Pattern 2: qa/e2e/e2e_assertions.sh (195 lines) ----
//
// Line 10-32: e2e_assert_exit_code. Line 37-62: e2e_assert_stdout_match.
// Line 67-91: e2e_assert_stderr_match. Line 96-126: e2e_assert_json_valid
// (jq or python3 -m json.tool). Line 131-158: e2e_assert_c_emit_contains
// (oodac emit-c + grep). Line 163-195: e2e_assert_no_gcc_spawn
// (shadow gcc, PATH hijack). Imported by e2e_harness_common.sh:191.
//
// ---- Pattern 3: tier master runners (4 files) ----
//
// qa/e2e/01_tier1_feature_coverage/01_tier1_coverage.sh
// qa/e2e/02_tier2_boundary_corner/                (master absent or 01_tier2_*)
// qa/e2e/03_tier3_pairwise_combinations/01_tier3_pairwise.sh
// qa/e2e/04_tier4_real_world_scenarios/01_tier4_workloads.sh
// Sample (qa/e2e/03_tier3_pairwise_combinations/01_tier3_pairwise.sh:1-18):
// sources harness, loops `for tscript in $SCRIPT_DIR/t3_*.sh; do bash; done`.
// Pure orchestrator.
//
// ---- Pattern 4: tier 1-4 individual test scripts (~152 files) ----
//
// Sample (qa/e2e/01_tier1_feature_coverage/t1_f01_01_outline_plaintext_basic.sh:1-19):
//   #!/usr/bin/env bash
//   set -euo pipefail
//   SCRIPT_DIR=...; source e2e_harness_common.sh
//   FIXTURE=$E2E_TEST_SCRATCH/test_fn.oo
//   cat << 'EOF' > "$FIXTURE"
//   pub fn main() { }
//   pub fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int { return a + b }
//   EOF
//   run_e2e_cmd_dual "T1-F01-01" 0 "fn main" "" "$OODA_BIN" outline "$FIXTURE"
//
// Uniform shape: source harness, write fixture (heredoc or copy
// from $OODA_SRC_ROOT/.../real_world/), run_e2e_cmd_dual.
//
// Spreads:
//   t1_f01_* (outline), t1_f02_* (reflect), t1_f03_* (python-free),
//   t1_f04_* (refcount), t1_f05_* (scope-drop), t1_f06_* (fuzz),
//   t1_f08_* (wasm), t1_f10_* (llvm), t1_f13_* (jit vm).
//   t2_f01_*..t2_f02_* (boundary: empty, syntax error, unreadable,
//     large file, special chars).
//   t3_01..09 (pairwise: reflect+raii, wasm+scope-drop, llvm+ast,
//     jit+contract, contract+scope, python-free+wasm, etc).
//   t4_01..07 (real-world: web router, wasm matrix, crypto wallet,
//     llvm pipeline, refactoring bot, cross-compiler, self-host).
//
// ---- Pattern 5: qa/tests_security/meta_path_a_hide_rail.sh (86 lines) ----
//
// Line 5-9: ROOT/OODA/OODAC/SCR setup.
// Line 25-27: `oodac emit-c $ON >meta_on.c 2>meta_on.err`.
// Line 28-33: `grep -c 'static void __oo_meta_decoy_' meta_on.c`.
// Line 51-61: same emit, assert zero decoys for off fixture.
// Line 63-79: shell to `ooda/scripts/oo_hide_smoke.sh` (another .sh).
// Line 82-85: exit 1 on any bad.
//
// Asserts compiler emit invariants (decoy on/off), not runtime smoke.
// Same .oo port pattern: process_exec oodac, fs_write fixture,
// str_contains on the C output.
//
// ---- Pattern 6: tree-sitter/grammar_smoke.sh (16 lines) ----
//
// Line 1: `#!/usr/bin/env bash`.
// Line 3: `set -euo pipefail`.
// Line 6: `node parse_probe.js corpus/valid.oo corpus/invalid.oo`.
// Line 7-10: `grep -q 'parse_rd' parse_probe.js` (must NOT match).
// Line 11-15: `command -v npx` probe (informational).
//
// Tests a third-party Node tool (tree-sitter), not OODA product.
// tree-sitter/ is an external grammar directory. RULES 1.13
// (RULES.oot:75-91) is directory-blind, so the file still violates
// it. But the fix is a move, not a port.

// =====================================================================
// 4. THREE OPTIONS PER PATTERN
// =====================================================================
//
// (a) CONVERT to .oo. Source stays at qa/e2e/.../*.oo.
//     Runtime: process_exec("ooda", ...) for the binary.
//     Fixture: fs_write($E2E_TEST_SCRATCH/file.oo, heredoc).
//     Assertion: str_contains(grep) via .oo string ops.
//     Harness exports become .oo pub fns in ooda/scripts/*_harness.oo
//     (or qa/e2e/*_harness.oo). Each test imports the harness.
//     Cost: ~1500 lines of .oo port, mechanically translated.
//
// (b) MOVE to a non-product path: .scripts/e2e/*.sh (top-level,
//     dotfile-prefix; default find ignores it), or scripts/e2e/*.sh
//     (top-level; explicit allow-list), or qa/.scripts/*.sh.
//     All need a RULES 1.13 amendment in WORKFLOW.oot naming the
//     .sh sub-tree. RULES.oot is immutable (RULES.oot:3).
//     Cost: a RULES amendment + mv + new top-level path.
//
// (c) DOCUMENT EXEMPTION per file. WORKFLOW.oot §X lists each .sh
//     with a one-line justification. dinner_lint gets a per-path
//     allow-list mirroring `! -name 'oodac_pure_build'` on
//     dinner_lint.oo:21.
//     Cost: a 168-row inventory table in WORKFLOW.oot. Maintenance
//     sink; silently admits new violations.

// =====================================================================
// 5. RECOMMENDED OPTION PER PATTERN
// =====================================================================
//
// | Pattern | Rec  | Why                                                     |
// | 1 (harness_common)        | (a) | Counters, mktemp, grep map to .oo primitives.       |
// | 2 (assertions)            | (a) | Six pure helpers; shadow-gcc = fs_write + PATH via   |
// |                           |     | process_exec env.                                     |
// | 3 (tier master runners)   | (a) | Loop-and-bash; .oo port is a list walked with        |
// |                           |     | sys_exec per item.                                    |
// | 4 (tier 1-4 individuals)  | (a) | Mechanical 1:1 port; 15-40 lines each.              |
// | 5 (meta_path_a_hide_rail) | (a) | emit-c + grep + assert. oo_hide_smoke.sh on line 63 |
// |                           |     | becomes process_exec ooda/scripts/oo_hide_smoke.oo.  |
// | 6 (tree-sitter grammar)   | (b) | Tests a Node tool, not product. Move to              |
// |                           |     | tree-sitter/.scripts/grammar_smoke.sh beside         |
// |                           |     | parse_probe.js. One-line WORKFLOW.oot entry.         |
//
// All (a) conversions land under ooda/scripts/qa_*.oo, matching
// RULES.oot:89 ("ooda/scripts/*.oo — pure .oo proofs, smokes,
// fixers, and tools"). dinner_lint.oo:21 already covers ooda/.
//
// (c) is rejected as the default: 168 rows is a maintenance sink.
// (c) may apply in narrow future cases (e.g., a bash-only POSIX
// toolchain shim), with one WORKFLOW.oot row each.

// =====================================================================
// 6. DINNER_LINT SCOPE FIX (DEPENDENCY)
// =====================================================================
//
// dinner_lint.oo:21 and dinner_lint.oo:24 currently use:
//
//   find openOODA ooda docs openOODA.github.io
//
// qa/ is missing. Add qa/ to the find target on those two lines.
// dinner_lint.oo:28 already lists `qa` in the header-check loop,
// so only the file-extension and line-limit checks need qa/ added.
// After the fix, any new .sh under qa/ fails closed on the next
// dinner_lint run.

// =====================================================================
// 7. ACCEPTANCE TEST
// =====================================================================
//
// 1. RULES 1.13 satisfied.
//    a. find qa -name '*.sh'           returns 0 lines.
//    b. find tree-sitter -name '*.sh'  returns 0 lines.
//    c. openOODA/scripts/dinner_lint.oo exit 0.
//
// 2. dinner_lint scope widened.
//    a. openOODA/scripts/dinner_lint.oo:21 and :24 list `qa`.
//    b. Re-run dinner_lint.oo: still exit 0 with new scope.
//
// 3. Harness parity.
//    a. ooda/scripts/qa_e2e_harness.oo   exists; exports the same
//       six helpers + three legacy helpers as e2e_harness_common.sh
//       and e2e_assertions.sh.
//    b. ooda/scripts/qa_tier{1,2,3,4}_runner.oo exist; reproduce
//       the 4 master runners.
//    c. ooda/scripts/qa_tier{1,2,3,4}_*.oo exist; one per individual
//       t?_* script, totaling ~152.
//    d. ooda/scripts/qa_meta_path_a_hide_rail.oo exists; reproduces
//       qa/tests_security/meta_path_a_hide_rail.sh.
//
// 4. (b) move path kept honest.
//    a. tree-sitter/.scripts/grammar_smoke.sh  is the single .sh.
//    b. openOODA/WORKFLOW.oot has a one-line entry naming
//       `tree-sitter/.scripts/` as a third-party smoke allow-list.
//
// 5. INT proof.
//    a. ooda ooda/scripts/qa_tier1_runner.oo                exit 0.
//    b. ooda ooda/scripts/qa_tier2_runner.oo                exit 0.
//    c. ooda ooda/scripts/qa_tier3_runner.oo                exit 0.
//    d. ooda ooda/scripts/qa_tier4_runner.oo                exit 0.
//    e. ooda ooda/scripts/qa_meta_path_a_hide_rail.oo       exit 0.
//    f. tree-sitter/.scripts/grammar_smoke.sh              exit 0.
//    g. openOODA/scripts/dinner_lint.oo                    exit 0.
//
// 6. Rollback.
//    a. Each .oo port is in its own file; `git checkout HEAD -- <oo>`
//       reverts one file without touching siblings.
//    b. The dinner_lint.oo:21 / :24 scope change is one edit per
//       line; revertable in a single commit.
//
// residual: this handoff names a port job, not new product code.
// Compiler, library, and C-runtime lanes stay untouched. No board
// edits until §7 acceptance passes.
